        "body": "<!-- proofline:finding-series=01a202cd-2d0c-7442-a42c-8fbe279c41fc -->\n**Warning** \u00b7 Concurrent console commands can abort during the schema upgrade\n\nTwo commands can both read `user_version` as `1`; after one commits migration `002`, the other still attempts to create the same index.\n\nThe second command exits with an index-already-exists error before dispatch.\n\nAcquire a write transaction before reading `user_version` and apply pending migrations within that transaction.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Details</summary>\n\nThe duplicate-index failure on version-1 databases did not exist before this change. The base had an analogous startup race when creating the initial tables on a new database.\n\n</details>\n\n[View finding in Proofline](https://proofline.sh/orgs/by-id/01a202a0-cd61-7684-99bc-53c775b0de50/reviews/01a202cb-ac5f-769c-a172-7242b7b635c2/findings/01a202cd-2d11-7012-be62-7007f30adb6a)\n\nAlso at:\n- [`console.py`](https://github.com/Pratik8445/bench-run-coderabbit/blob/68ef658388c5cc9ec890d030918fb6a0b36ea369/console.py#L29-L37) lines 29 to 37",
